{"requirements":[{"id":"fifo-reconnection-and-recording","requirement":"The consumer must remain running across successive producer disconnects, append every complete non-empty newline-delimited job ID, and retain existing records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original previous-job record remained. Two separate producer sessions were accepted by the same consumer PID, the submitted blank line was omitted, and all non-empty jobs were appended in order. Source inspection also shows buffering until a newline is received.","evidence_ids":["cmd-663a6c378990478c","cmd-cdc2ea56435b428c","cmd-ea79adfe4def46a5","cmd-ee549d79d9204c4d"]},{"id":"idle-without-busy-loop","requirement":"The consumer must avoid a busy loop while no producer is connected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live consumer accumulated zero CPU jiffies during a four-second producer-free interval; its select-based implementation waits with a timeout.","evidence_ids":["cmd-663a6c378990478c","cmd-8010e0de15674793"]},{"id":"clean-sigterm-shutdown","requirement":"The consumer must shut down cleanly on SIGTERM without damaging retained records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Service stop completed in one second, the prior PID exited, the record count remained unchanged, and a subsequent start was healthy. The service's five-second TERM grace period supports that this was a graceful TERM exit rather than forced KILL.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7403e1cb3be942f4","cmd-354f0e4885cb4aba"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained Alpine Linux 3.23 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after the work and reboot. Python 3.12.15 was installed from the configured Alpine 3.23 repositories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fbfbef10ad074da2","cmd-53fef17c08f94a92","cmd-c9288c6a556f4fa0","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"The implementation and validation mutations were causally related to the task, and package health and exposed listening sockets showed no concerning degradation. Two low-risk hygiene issues remain: cmd-1f930706aafb4ca9 temporarily replaced consumer.py with syntactically invalid content before the next command corrected it, and it created consumer.py.pre-repair with no later removal shown; the backup therefore appears to remain as abandoned residue. The mandatory reboot command also left /tmp/fifo-worker-reboot.log behind. The malformed consumer change was reverted; the backup and temporary reboot log were not shown cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f930706aafb4ca9","cmd-663a6c378990478c","cmd-ffb905c6ec7646fc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, reboot was acknowledged, the independently cross-checked boot ID changed, the service recovered automatically, prior data persisted, and a post-reboot job was consumed successfully.","limitations":["There was no behavioral probe specifically splitting one job line across multiple writes or producer connections; that case is supported by direct inspection of the pending-buffer implementation rather than an observed test.","The lifecycle collector cannot report failed OpenRC services because its failed-service probe is systemd-specific; the fifo-worker service itself was nevertheless directly verified as started before and after reboot.","No final directory inventory was captured, so retention of consumer.py.pre-repair is inferred from its creation and the absence of any subsequent removal command."]}
